<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Confusion</h1>
<p>Sphere: Mind Sphere
Spell Tier: 1
Class: Sorcerer (guild level 13, up to 80%)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast confusion &lt;target&gt;
</pre>
<p>The caster thrusts a clawed hand at the target and screams 'Suino fanoc!', 
and the target's mind is muddled for as long as the confusion lasts: from 
a minute up to several minutes, the better your spell. While it lasts:
</p>
<ul><li>each move has a one in three chance to go out another open exit instead, chosen at random ("In your confusion you stumble the wrong way");</li>
<li>each spell has a one in four chance to fizzle before it starts, costing no mana ("You lose your train of thought");</li>
<li>a monster that is hunting someone, tracking them through the world, loses the trail and gives up the hunt.</li></ul>
<p>Use it to shake off a monster that follows you after you have fled, or to 
muddle a foe. It doesn't stop a fight.
</p><p>The target resists with its mind; if the spell fails, it attacks you. You 
must be standing. Confusion shows among the spells on you (<a cmd='#'>affect</a>). It 
is also found on potions, wands, staffs and scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Fleeing</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Mind Sphere</a>
</pre>




</div>